content:
{
  "email": "sofia.rossi@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Identify sender, account, and devices for vague computer issue report"
}

{
  "hostname": "BL-LT-0107",
  "reason": "Check laptop health for clues to the recurring issue"
}

{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Sofia, sorry your computer is acting up again. I'd like to help, but I need a bit more detail first. Could you tell me: 1) What exactly happens? For example, is it slow or freezing, showing an error message (please copy the exact wording or send a screenshot), crashing or showing a blue screen, or giving you trouble signing in? 2) When did it start this time, and how often does it happen? 3) When did you last fully restart the laptop? Closing the lid doesn't count. 4) Did it start after an update or after you installed something new? Also, our records show your laptop hasn't connected to our management system in about 12 days. Is the laptop with you and working, and is it connected to the internet or VPN? If it's been lost or stolen, please tell us right away. Once I hear back, I can get this sorted out quickly.",
  "internal_note": "The ticket is vague: 'my computer is doing the thing again.' The user account is active, not locked, 0 failed sign-ins, not VIP. Her only device is BL-LT-0107 (Win11). It is offline, with last check-in 2026-09-29 and a warning of no check-in for 12 days. Disk is fine (54.7% free), so low disk space isn't the cause. Possible causes: the device has been offline or off the network a long time, the management agent is broken, or the device is lost (nothing suggests that). No previous ticket history was available to me, so I can't tell what 'the thing' is. I asked the user for symptoms, timing, last restart, and recent changes, and asked her to confirm she has the device. Once she replies, follow KB-019 if it's slowness or freezing. Escalate if it's crashes or blue screens, if the device is lost (KB-021, P1), or if no article covers the problem.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-019"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
